<<Reset>>
<<Scene #000000 0.985>>

<<LookAt 3 7>>
<<Act Zoran zoranSmug 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: Ah, yes, the very backbone of any conflict, territory. 
<<Act Zoran zoranTalk 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: It is not enough to simply exist upon the land, Your Majesty. One must own it.

Zoran: The realm is dotted with various settlements, each with its own… purpose.
<<Act Zoran zoranChill 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: Some are useful. Some are liabilities. But all are pieces on the board.

<<Scene #000000 0.585>>
<<LookAt 6 7>>
Zoran: This, for instance, is a <b>small town</b>. A quaint little cluster of hovels and dreams.
<<Act Zoran zoranTalk 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: It generates a respectable number of troops.
<<Act Zoran zoranSmug 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
<<Scene #000000 0.985>>
Zoran: But, alas, much like its inhabitants, it is fragile.
Zoran: The enemy can seize it without much trouble.

<<Scene #000000 0.585>>
<<LookAt 5 7>>
<<Act Zoran zoranTalk 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: A large town provides more troops, which is lovely.
<<Act Zoran zoranTalk 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: But, much like its smaller counterpart, it remains… exposed. If you do not defend it, the enemy will gladly take it off your hands.

<<Act Zoran zoranSurprise 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
<<LookAt 3 7>>
Zoran: Ah, but this! <br>This is a castle.
<<Act Zoran zoranTalk 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: Unlike those flimsy towns, castles are built to last.
<<Act Zoran zoranSmug 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: Taking one is an ordeal, an unpleasant, drawn out mess that can cost the enemy double the troops it has stationed inside to take it off your hands.
Zoran: They do not produce any troops, unlike towns, but what does it matter? 
<<Act Zoran zoranTalk 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: A wise ruler knows how to restation troops where they are needed most.

<<Act Zoran zoranChill 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: Keep these in mind, Your Majesty.

<<Act Zoran zoranSmug 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: …And you may prove yourself worthy of the throne.

<<StopAudioAll>>
<<Reset>>
<<stop>>

